    "conclusion": "Provenance CONTEXT was recovered for 77 of 110 assets: which picture each one is, which Discovery it served, and the commit and date that introduced it. Provenance CLASSIFICATION was recovered for NONE. No deployed image carries any evidence of what made it, so no image is declared. Nine masters in the library DO carry iOS device evidence and are therefore photographs, but not one of them is among the assets that shipped.",
    "a_fourth_class_may_be_needed": "Those nine masters are photographs taken by PlotNua. They are neither a supplier's image nor an AI illustration, so the approved three-state taxonomy has no place for a first-party photograph. None of them is published today, so nothing is blocked -- but the first one to be published will need a founder decision rather than a guess. Recorded here rather than resolved, because inventing a class was not authorised."
